[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Not Very Musical]
[00:15.28]What happened when the snake charmer began to play jazz?
[00:23.18]As we had had a long walk through one of the markets of old Delhi,
[00:29.16]we stopped at a square to have a rest.
[00:33.36]After a time, we noticed a snake charmer with two large baskets at the other side of the square,
[00:41.87]so we went to have a look at him.
[00:45.04]As soon as he saw us,
[00:47.45]he picked up a long pipe which was covered with coins and opened one of the baskets.
[00:56.15]When he began to play a tune,
[00:59.03]we had our first glimpse of the snake.
[01:03.44]It rose out of the basket and began to follow the movements of the pipe.
[01:10.40]We were very much surprised when the snake charmer
[01:14.56]suddenly began to play jazz and modern pop songs.
[01:20.68]The snake, however, continued to 'dance' slowly.
[01:26.52]It obviously could not tell the difference between Indian music and jazz!
